      "section_changes": {
        "Remarks": {
          "before": null,
          "after": "The supplied orientation makes both nonzero rows constant-coefficient rows.\nOn page $n+1$, the following schematic shows two columns of these rows;\nall intermediate rows are zero. Here $a\\geq0$ and the diagonal arrow has\nbidegree $(n+1,-n)$.\n\n```tikzcd\n[font=\\Large, labels={font=\\large}, row sep=3em, column sep=4em]\nE_{n+1}^{a,n}=H^a(B;R)u \\arrow[dr, \"d_{n+1}\" description] & E_{n+1}^{a+n+1,n}=H^{a+n+1}(B;R)u \\\\\nE_{n+1}^{a,0}=H^a(B;R) & E_{n+1}^{a+n+1,0}=H^{a+n+1}(B;R)\n```\n\nFor $x\\in H^a(B;R)$ the diagonal sends $xu$ to\n$(-1)^a x\\smile e(p)$; at $a=0$ it sends $u$ to $e(p)$.\nTaking its cokernels in the bottom row and kernels in the top row gives the\ntwo stable terms of proof step 3.1. Their short exact filtration sequence\nthen gives (1): $p^*$ factors through the bottom-row cokernel, while $p_!$\nis the top-row quotient followed by its inclusion, using the orientation,\ninto $H^{k-n}(B;R)$. The cup maps in (1) retain its stated sign normalization.\nThe schematic neither asserts a splitting of the filtration nor identifies\n$p_!$ with a cohomological axis edge; the proof above is independent of it."
        }
      },
